 extra=[
 ('compare','A publisher provides a trusted digest for its original file. Your computer calculates a digest for the download. What should happen next?','Compare the two digest values','Decrypt the digest to open the file|Assume the filename proves safety|Treat the digest as a password for the publisher','The useful operation is comparison. Different digest values show different contents; a match is meaningful only when the reference is trusted.'),
 ('alone','A program displays a file’s hash value, but you have no trusted reference. Does that value alone tell you the file is the publisher’s genuine release?','No; the value alone does not establish a trusted match or publisher identity','Yes; any displayed hash proves the file is genuine|Yes; the letters and digits identify every publisher|Yes; hashing makes every file safe','A digest is calculated from contents. Without a trusted comparison or appropriate authentication, displaying it does not identify the publisher or certify safety.'),
 ('mismatch','Your computed digest differs from the trusted original digest. What should you conclude about the contents?','They differ; investigate or obtain the correct file before relying on it','The file was successfully decrypted|Both files must be identical|The digest automatically repairs the file','A mismatch is useful evidence of different contents. It does not repair the download or explain whether the difference came from corruption, editing, or an attacker.'),
 ]
